{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["And I say — R. Marinus said: that it stands in place of ויאמר, and the like is not found in the sacred language. The correct interpretation: that the prophet said, after they removed the filthy garments and clothed him in festive garments, how fine it would be if a pure turban were on his head. Or the word ואומר means \"this [I said] in my heart\" — thus I thought in my heart, and I saw that my thought was fulfilled, and behold the pure turban was set on his head. And they had already clothed him in garments. Similarly: וירם תולעים ויבאש — and it already bred maggots, for everything first rots and afterward breeds maggots."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The verse quotation וירם תולעים ויבאש appears to allude to the manna narrative (Exodus 16:20); the text as given reads literally 'and it bred maggots and rotted,' and the final clause explaining the sequence of rotting preceding maggots seems to reverse the order in the quotation itself. Left hyper-literal; possible textual corruption."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:50.620837523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}